  "summary": "A turboexpander lets high-pressure gas expand through a radial-inflow turbine wheel. Because the gas does work on the wheel, its temperature drops far more than in a valve — the basis of gas processing, air separation and LNG refrigeration. The recovered power drives a compressor wheel on the same shaft (or a generator). Variable inlet guide vanes control the flow.",
